{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The portable SSD fits my computer-focused purchases because I can use it for backups and moving files between computers without needing a separate storage installation.",
    "The over-ear headphones fit my desk listening setup and headphone mount, while the microSD card could support my Raspberry Pi projects after I check compatibility."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming sticks, smart display, and security cameras introduce activities I have not shown a current need for; owning electronics does not mean I am setting up streaming or a connected home.",
    "Earbuds do not serve the desk-listening need that makes the over-ear headphones appealing, and the enterprise hard drive requires a storage project and compatible hardware I have not established."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical computer equipment seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any electronic gadget.",
    "My headphone and memory-card purchases seem to have been treated as reasons to suggest any audio or storage product, even when its intended use and setup requirements differ."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases connect around organizing, maintaining, and using a computer workspace: Ethernet connections, cable management, cleaning equipment, and a headphone mount.",
    "Compatibility and purpose matter to me: a card for my Raspberry Pi needs checking separately from my Garmin card, and portable file storage serves a different need from a large internal enterprise drive."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my computer and desk needs but extended that interest too broadly to unrelated electronics."
}"}
